{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788190103,"nonce":"X7fNx05H1yQ8QHFvzgeL0iN660E=","title":"No verb can use a targetable item on a target — resurrector serums, shock lances, EMP are unreachable","message":"Found by play, 2026-08-31. Evan asked for a resurrector serum to be used on a\ndead colonist. There is no route.\n\nThe verb surface has exactly one item-use verb, `consume`, and it is INGEST\n(food, drugs, medicine). Everything whose use is \"select the item, then click a\ntarget\" has no verb at all:\n\n- `MechSerumResurrector` — on a corpse (the case that surfaced this)\n- `MechSerumHealer`\n- psychic shock lance / insanity lance — on a pawn\n- EMP / smoke / firefoam poppers thrown at a position\n- `GhoulResurrectionSerum` (Anomaly)\n\nThese are `CompUsable` / `CompTargetable` items: the float-menu option comes\nfrom the comp, the pawn must be carrying the item, and the order is a job with\na target. That is a THIRD order shape the mod does not model — it has \"order a\npawn to do work on a thing\" (`prioritize`, `orders`) and \"order a pawn to a\ncell\" (`move-to`), but not \"order a pawn to apply a carried item to a target\".\n\nWHAT TO INVESTIGATE BEFORE BUILDING\n\n- `RimWorld/CompUsable.cs` and `CompTargetable` and its subclasses\n  (`CompTargetable_SingleCorpse`, `CompTargetable_SinglePawn`, …) — each defines\n  what it may be aimed at, and that IS the widget gate to reproduce.\n- The float-menu provider that offers these options, and its preconditions:\n  the item must be reachable or carried, the target must satisfy the comp's\n  validator, and the pawn must be capable.\n- Whether the resulting job is `JobDefOf.UseItem` (check) and what it takes as\n  targetA/targetB.\n- Whether `orders {pawn, thing}` already surfaces any of this — it reproduces\n  the WORK-GIVER menu, which is a different menu from the float menu these\n  options live on. Establish that boundary explicitly; it is probably why this\n  was never noticed.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND THE ONE ITEM\n\nResurrection is the difference between losing a colonist permanently and not,\nand healer serums are the answer to a permanent injury. An agent running a\nlong game that cannot use them is playing with one hand tied. The lances and\ngrenade-poppers are tactical options that a combat-capable agent should have.\n\nAcceptance\n\n- A verb that orders a pawn to use a carried targetable item on a target,\n  plural-first like the rest of the action surface.\n- The gate is the comp's own validator, cited by FILE + MEMBER, and a target the\n  comp refuses is rejected with a named gate rather than attempted.\n- The pawn not carrying the item is its own named refusal, distinct from an\n  invalid target.\n- Demonstrated live: a resurrector serum used on a colonist corpse, and the\n  pawn is alive afterwards with `ResurrectionSickness` present.\n- A read that lists what a carried item may legitimately be used on, so the\n  agent can ask before ordering (mirrors `orders` / `surgery-options`).","files":null}]}